# courier-outbox core

Reliable outbound webhook delivery in Go: Postgres outbox, SKIP LOCKED workers, HMAC-signed POSTs, retries 1s→5s→25s→2m→10m, DLQ, idempotent enqueue. Delivery is **at-least-once**, never exactly-once.

## Before writing code
- Read `AGENTS.md`, then the relevant doc in `docs/architecture/`.
- Non-trivial behaviour (endpoint, table, config var, delivery/signing/SSRF semantics) requires an approved Fission OpenSpec change (`/opsx-propose` → `openspec/changes/<id>/`). Implement only what the change lists (`/opsx-apply`).

## Layout (fixed - do not invent new top-level internal packages without an ADR)
- `cmd/courier` composition root · `internal/api` HTTP · `internal/domain` pure model · `internal/store` Postgres/Redis + TX · `internal/worker` delivery loop + outbound client · `internal/sign` HMAC · `internal/config` env · `migrations/` forward-only SQL · `openapi/` contract.
- Dependency rule: domain imports no internal package; api/worker depend on interfaces they declare; store implements them; cmd wires.

## Git
- Conventional, small commits: `feat(scope):`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:`, `ci:`, `refactor:`.
- Author/committer is the repo owner's configured identity. Never add agent/bot authors or AI `Co-authored-by` trailers.
- Never commit secrets; update `.env.example` (placeholders only) when adding config.

## Definition of done
- `go build ./...`, `go test -race ./...`, `golangci-lint run` green.
- `openapi/openapi.yaml` updated with any HTTP change; tests cover error paths.
- OpenSpec tasks ticked; change archived after merge.
